---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '28 July 2026';

/**
 * Terms for the WEBSITE only. Nothing here is the software licence — that is a signed
 * agreement, and saying so explicitly is the point of the first section. A prospect's legal
 * team reading website terms that appear to govern the product is a real problem.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website terms"
  description="The terms that apply to this website. They are not the software agreement — that is signed separately."
>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <span class="eyebrow text-accent-onDark tick-on-dark">Terms</span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-display-sm md:text-display-md leading-tight">
        Terms for this website.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-muted-onDark">Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-10 text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">These are not the software terms</h2>
        <p>
          This page governs your use of <span class="font-semibold text-white">mesvantage.com</span>
          and nothing else. Use of the MESvantage software is governed by a separate written
          agreement signed by both parties, which covers licensing, service levels, data
          ownership, data processing, validation support, change control and termination. If
          anything on this website conflicts with that agreement, that agreement wins. Nothing
          published here forms part of it and nothing here is an offer capable of acceptance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          MESvantage Limited, a company registered in Ireland. Contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@mesvantage.com" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white"
            >hello@mesvantage.com</a
          >. Where our registered number and registered office are shown, they appear in the
          footer of every page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What we intend the content to do</h2>
        <p>
          The purpose of this site is to let you evaluate whether MESvantage is worth a
          conversation, and to let you check our claims rather than take them on trust. To that
          end:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>
            Every figure we publish is listed on the
            <a href="/evidence" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white">evidence register</a>
            with its source, method and the date it was last verified — or with an explicit note
            that the supporting artefact does not exist yet.
          </li>
          <li>
            Screen images are captures of the real application running against a seeded
            demonstration dataset for a fictional manufacturer. They are labelled as such, with
            the route, the build and the capture date. They are not customer records.
          </li>
          <li>
            Capabilities described as planned are labelled as planned, and the things we do not
            have are listed on
            <a href="/limits" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white">a page of their own</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Where we describe outcomes, they are descriptions of what the software does, not
          guarantees of the result you will get. Your results depend on your processes, your
          data and your own validation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Nothing here is regulatory advice</h2>
        <p>
          We write about ISO 13485, 21 CFR Part 11, the FDA QMSR and computer system validation
          because our customers work under them. None of it is legal or regulatory advice, and
          none of it changes your obligations. In particular, validating any software for its
          intended use within your quality system is your responsibility as the manufacturer and
          cannot be transferred to a supplier. We say this on the compliance page, on the limits
          page and here, because it is the single most commonly oversold point in this market.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The content, design and software behind this site belong to MESvantage Limited or its
          licensors. You may read it, print it, and quote it for the purpose of evaluating or
          discussing MESvantage, including internally and including in a written recommendation
          against us. Please quote accurately and link back. You may not republish it as your
          own or use it to train a model for a competing product.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We try to keep this site up and correct, and we will fix errors when we find them or
          when you point them out. We do not promise the site will be uninterrupted, and we may
          change or withdraw any page. Availability commitments for the software live in the
          signed agreement, not here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for loss arising from
          reliance on this website's content. We do not exclude or limit liability for death or
          personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or
          for anything else that cannot lawfully be excluded — including any right you have as a
          consumer under Irish or EU law.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Links out</h2>
        <p>
          Where we link to standards bodies, regulators or third-party sources, we do it so you
          can check us. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of Ireland, and the courts of Ireland have
          exclusive jurisdiction. If you are a consumer, this does not deprive you of the
          protection of the mandatory law of the country in which you live.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we change these terms we will change the date at the top. We do not keep a public
          history of this page; we do keep one for the
          <a href="/evidence" class="text-accent-onDark font-semibold hover:text-white">evidence register</a>,
          which is the page where a change would actually matter to you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
